{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF30", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF30 | Study family SF30: Brown to Tatum matched causal sequence test\n- observed_research_question: Brown to Tatum matched causal sequence test\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Jaylen Brown involvement raises PPP on Tatum's next BOS possession beyond matched state/opponent controls.\n- observed_result: Def A ATT -0.017, bootstrap CI [-0.092, +0.061], perm p=0.028. Def B ATT -0.077, CI [-0.146, -0.001]. Placebo mean ~0; real ATT inside placebo 95% range both defs. Signs flip across quarters/RS-PO.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: ATT not positive; does not separate from shuffled-Brown placebo; wrong-signed where 'significant'.\n- observed_sample_and_power: treated 1,173 (A) / 1,313 (B)\n- observed_method: PSM 1:3 caliper 0.05; Def A initiator (1173 treated / 5819 control); Def B event involvement; shuffled-Brown placebo.\n- observed_verdict: null"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-026", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-026 | Study family SF-CHT-026: League-wide PNR-fail to PULL_UP sequence branches\n- observed_research_question: League-wide PNR-fail to PULL_UP sequence branches\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: If PNR fail then PULL_UP is a real league-wide counter, it should show lift>0 in >=70% of units with median lift>2pp.\n- observed_result: Zero branches passed. The BOS-MIA PNR to PULL_UP dyad was matchup-specific.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Zero branches passed the >=70% units / median lift>2pp rule.\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Branch search across teams/series for the BOS-MIA PNR to PULL_UP dyad.\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: B_powered_null\n- observed_notes: Chat-only summary of the branch search; no separate path quoted beyond the conversation.\n- auto_confidence: high (0.8)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-088"}, {"id": "FAM:SF09", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF09 | Study family SF09: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- observed_research_question: Double-suppression stacking (POST_UP then PUTBACK)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: Opponent POST_UP then PUTBACK stacks additively against the next star possession.\n- observed_result: [APPA-057] Baseline 1.210 n=960,764. After PUTBACK only 1.097 d=-0.113 n=15,898. After POST_UP only 1.091 d=-0.119 n=76,329. Stacked 1.138 d=-0.071 n=1,047 vs additive prediction -0.232. Mitchell after PUTBACK 0.919 vs 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- observed_result: [APPS-042] POST_UP Q1->Q4 -0.065 (Q1 -0.119 to Q4 -0.184); PUTBACK -0.374 (0.144 to -0.23). TRANSITION cluster gradient +0.075 (unexpected vs hypothesized flat). Stacked delta -0.071 vs additive prediction -0.232 (less t [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: none (no failure recorded)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:implementation_bug\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:IMPLEMENTATION_BUG"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-024 | Study family SF-APPS-024: DRIVE-as-BEST counter vs constrained mix\n- observed_research_question: DRIVE-as-BEST counter vs constrained mix\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: When BEST=DRIVE (counter_h2_n>=5), observed DRIVE H2 PPP beats a feasibility-constrained baseline.\n- observed_result: A mean=1.178 vs B_game 1.236 (gap=-0.058, p=0.6069) vs B_fixed 1.244 (gap=-0.066, p=0.2175) vs coach default C 1.134 (gap=+0.043, p=0.3052). MDE at 80% power ~0.180 PPP (SD~0.34).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_power_large_MDE\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Observed gap -0.066 is below MDE 0.180; n=44 cannot distinguish a true null from an effect up to 0.18 PPP.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=44; MDE 0.180 PPP at 80% power (SD~0.34); 0.265 if SD~0.5\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
